  "primary_task": "contrast_flow_analysis",
  "other_label": null,
  "secondary_tasks": ["vessel_segmentation"],
  "task_description": "Automatic computation of coronary flow reserve (CFRauto) from paired rest and hyperemic coronary angiograms: a modified U-Net segments the main coronary artery in every frame, centerline length over time yields a length/time curve whose slope during contrast injection gives flow velocity; CFR is the hyperemic-to-rest velocity ratio, compared with manual TIMI frame count CFR. Segmentation evaluated by 5-fold cross-validation (development cohort of 2407 patients); CFRauto validated on an independent sample of 149 vessels from 138 patients.",
  "clinical_application": "Wire-free assessment of coronary microcirculatory function (coronary flow reserve) in the catheterization laboratory"
 },
